Touching this file starts .github/workflows/oos-harvest-and-evaluate.yml.
The workflow lives only on this research branch, and GitHub offers
workflow_dispatch only for workflows on the default branch, so a gated push
trigger is how a branch-local workflow gets started without touching main.

The two directives below are the only lines the workflow reads, and it matches
them anchored at both ends so this prose cannot be mistaken for one.

  - stage "harvest" reads all 46 post-cutoff hourly parts off the recorder's
    volume (read-only) and reduces each one to BTC 15m rows;
  - stage "evaluate" merges one named harvest, checks completeness, builds the
    OOS state table and runs the FROZEN 2939ee67 / c31a5e32 evaluation. It is
    requested exactly once.

STAGE=calibrate
HARVEST_RUN_ID=37230639101

Cutoff: cpc-btc-updown-15m-2026-10-02-2045z. Development ends at the cutoff;
only windows starting strictly after it are OOS.

REQUEST=5
